WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:05.640
Groot is many things: wise beyond his words,
adorable in his baby form, and a true team

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:06.160
player.

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:11.280
And, as seemingly evidenced in Avengers: Infinity
War, Groot is also as worthy as the God of

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:13.720
Thunder himself to wield an Asgardian weapon.

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:15.440
Or so it seems...

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:19.740
Infinity War co-directors Joe and Anthony
Russo have finally revealed how Groot was

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:22.020
able to lift Thor's new weapon in the film.

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:27.460
In Avengers: Infinity War, Thor, Groot, and
Rocket travel to Nidavellir to meet with Eitri,

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:32.430
the Asgardian Dwarf and weapons forger who
created Thor's fearsome Mjolnir - the hammer

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:36.000
that the Norse God's evil sister Hela destroyed
in Thor: Ragnarok.

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:39.820
"Darling, you have no idea what's possible"

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:48.140
After sparking up a dying star and reactivating
the forge to channel its raw energy, the foursome

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:53.300
craft Thor's new killer weapon: the hammer-meets-battle-ax
known as Stormbreaker.

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:55.880
The only thing missing from the weapon is
a handle.

00:00:55.960 --> 00:01:00.800
Groot steps up and sacrifices one of his arms
for the purpose, causing every viewer to let

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:05.500
out an "aww" at his act of bravery and at
the growing bond between the blonde-tressed

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:07.530
god and the tiny teen tree.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:12.680
But wait just a Marvel minute - if only those
who proved themselves worthy were able to

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:18.120
lift Thor's old weapon Mjolnir, how can Groot
pick up Thor's shiny new villain-slaying toy

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:18.620
Stormbreaker?

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:22.280
"Whosoever be he worthy shall haveth the power.

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:23.740
Whatever man it's a trick!"

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:28.000
Does that mean that Groot is on an equal playing
field as Thor in the eyes of the Asgardian

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.000
spirits?

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:32.680
As much as we love Groot, it turns out that
isn't the case.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:37.300
After a fan asked the Russo Brothers to explain
the scene, wondering whether Groot was suddenly

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:41.700
deemed worthy, the pair disclosed that Groot
was able to lift Stormbreaker because the

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:43.820
weapon doesn't have the same rules as Mjolnir.

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:45.320
The directors wrote on Twitter:

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:48.480
"Mjolnir requires worthiness, not Stormbreaker."

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:51.120
There's actually a bit of a catch when it
comes to this statement.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:55.860
Sure, anyone can pick up Stormbreaker regardless
of pre-determined suitability, but that doesn't

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:57.700
mean it's easy to lift the weapon.

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:01.960
With Mjolnir, it was about both worth and
physical strength - but it still wouldn't

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:05.980
budge unless someone deemed fit by the Asgardian
gods tried to lift it, no matter how buff

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:06.480
they were.

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:07.780
"We need to go."

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:17.720
With Stormbreaker, it's a different story.

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:22.160
Carrying such a special weapon is not only
a great responsibility, but it also requires

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:23.080
great power.

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:26.840
And let's remember that it isn't as though
Groot lifted Stormbreaker like it was a piece

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:28.980
of cosmic candy that had been dropped on the
ground.

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:33.019
He was in a great deal of pain as he wound
his arm around the weapons' two parts before

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:34.940
snapping it off to be used as a handle.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:40.080
While he appears to be as physically strong
as Thor, at least from this isolated incident,

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:44.060
Groot isn't invincible just because he can
lift the same weapon the Norse God can.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:48.800
However, Groot's ability to hold Stormbreaker
could signal something much bigger than simply

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:50.689
how powerful the Guardian is.

00:02:50.689 --> 00:02:55.499
There's a popular fan theory that suggests
Groot, who crumbled away into space dust after

00:02:55.499 --> 00:03:00.849
Thanos' culling at the end of Avengers: Infinity
War, will come back to life in Avengers 4,

00:03:00.849 --> 00:03:03.240
reborn through the wood in Stormbreaker.

00:03:03.569 --> 00:03:08.140
Groot sacrificed himself in the first Guardians
of the Galaxy, reemerging after death as an

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:08.660
infant.

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:13.240
Does that mean that he could perform another
self-resurrection in the upcoming Avengers

00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:13.740
movie?

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:17.660
It might sound like a long shot to some, but
Joe Russo, who directs Avengers 4 with his

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:20.240
brother Anthony, hasn't ruled it out completely.

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:22.260
The filmmaker told Huffington Post:

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:27.000
"I don't know if every piece of him that detaches
[…] can grow a future version of him, but

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:27.840
who's to say?

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:29.020
That's an interesting question."

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:33.269
Interesting enough to keep our minds busy
while we wait for Avengers 4 to drop?

00:03:33.269 --> 00:03:34.269
We think so.

00:03:34.269 --> 00:03:35.420
"I am groot!"

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:36.300
"Woah!"

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:36.800
"Language!"

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:37.360
"Hey!"

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:38.120
"Wow"

